WEBVTT

00:28.495 --> 00:32.261
Welcome to the battlefield,
Deca-Commander Abriel.

00:38.839 --> 00:41.933
Direct hit on enemy ship.
But there's only minimal damage.

00:58.392 --> 00:59.654
Engines, full power!

01:09.336 --> 01:10.325
Fire anti-proton cannon!

01:21.682 --> 01:23.775
Ten seconds to
space-time separation!

01:24.385 --> 01:28.355
Nine... eight... seven...
six... five...

01:28.355 --> 01:32.155
...four... three... two... one.

01:32.526 --> 01:33.515
Separation!

01:39.666 --> 01:40.360
Want one?

01:41.402 --> 01:42.926
Yes. I'll have one.

01:45.105 --> 01:48.108
I didn't think it was part of the
captain's job description...

01:48.108 --> 01:51.305
...to stand around watching
the repairs being done.

01:52.212 --> 01:53.611
Not because it's my duty.

01:53.981 --> 01:56.050
I'm not just trying to
make you feel better...

01:56.050 --> 01:58.452
...but looking at it objectively...

01:58.452 --> 02:01.755
Getting away with so little
damage on our first campaign...

02:01.755 --> 02:03.154
...we didn't do too badly.

02:03.424 --> 02:04.220
Don't you think?

02:05.692 --> 02:07.421
So you understand.

02:07.895 --> 02:08.987
Don't misunderstand.

02:09.863 --> 02:12.855
I just want to stand close by
the Basroil.

02:13.333 --> 02:15.369
I see. In that case...

02:15.369 --> 02:17.504
...I guess I'd better go and...

02:17.504 --> 02:19.734
...finish up what I have to do.

02:20.174 --> 02:22.972
So we can take a break together.

02:23.977 --> 02:25.706
Yes. You're right.

02:29.917 --> 02:31.151
Oh, right.

02:31.151 --> 02:33.915
There was something I wanted
to say to you before I go.

02:34.254 --> 02:35.346
What is it?

02:35.789 --> 02:39.589
You looked pretty good
on your first campaign, Captain.

02:40.060 --> 02:40.617
Fool.

02:44.465 --> 02:46.166
Imperial Calendar Year 955.

02:46.166 --> 02:49.169
The battleships
of the Star Forces...

02:49.169 --> 02:51.939
...had countered the advances
of the Triple Alliance...

02:51.939 --> 02:56.243
...which consisted of
the United Mankind...

02:56.243 --> 02:56.443
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

02:56.443 --> 02:59.379
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

02:59.379 --> 03:00.481
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

03:00.481 --> 03:02.108
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

03:02.649 --> 03:04.879
The counterattack had begun.

03:05.519 --> 03:06.353
As commander of the Third Fleet...

03:06.353 --> 03:08.255
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
As commander of the Third Fleet...

03:08.255 --> 03:12.626
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...as well as overall
commander-in-chief...

03:12.626 --> 03:13.794
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

03:13.794 --> 03:17.464
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

03:17.464 --> 03:18.232
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

03:18.232 --> 03:18.665
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

03:18.665 --> 03:19.600
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

03:19.600 --> 03:23.270
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

03:23.270 --> 03:23.504
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

03:23.504 --> 03:27.407
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

03:27.407 --> 03:28.208
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
Sparing nothing...

03:28.208 --> 03:28.642
Sparing nothing...

03:28.642 --> 03:32.913
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...to reorganize the fleet
in terms of scale...

03:32.913 --> 03:37.584
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

03:37.584 --> 03:40.144
Operation Phantom Flame.

03:40.954 --> 03:45.254
Now, the battle will truly begin.

03:53.400 --> 03:56.961
Spectacular Insanity

04:02.609 --> 04:07.637
Banner of the Stars

05:24.591 --> 05:27.321
Planet System Demetel

05:28.528 --> 05:31.632
Any changes to the situation?

05:31.632 --> 05:32.462
No.

05:32.866 --> 05:35.699
No movement since the enemy
reconnaissance missions.

05:36.036 --> 05:36.570
However...

05:36.570 --> 05:38.805
...given the information
they likely obtained...

05:38.805 --> 05:42.605
...they are surely proceeding with
preparations for a counterattack.

05:43.477 --> 05:45.879
Perhaps we underestimated them.

05:45.879 --> 05:49.249
This couldn't have come
at a worse time for us.

05:49.249 --> 05:50.307
I know.

05:51.318 --> 05:55.889
If the enemy had launched
their attack a little sooner...

05:55.889 --> 05:59.381
...our response to eliminate their
fleet would have been automatic.

06:00.060 --> 06:04.398
If they had the opportunity to
cut us off from the Aptic area...

06:04.398 --> 06:06.696
...we would surely
have faced defeat.

06:07.000 --> 06:09.136
Yes. On the other hand...

06:09.136 --> 06:10.771
...if they had decided to attack later...

06:10.771 --> 06:14.229
...then we would have advanced
from the front to the other side.

06:14.574 --> 06:17.477
Once we had completed the route
between...

06:17.477 --> 06:18.876
...Suruguzede and Laseesu...

06:19.279 --> 06:22.476
...we would've managed even if
they had cut our supply.

06:23.050 --> 06:24.318
In such a case...

06:24.318 --> 06:29.356
...my intention would have been to
attack them from both directions.

06:29.356 --> 06:32.484
But it seems the enemy was
more clever than that.

06:32.993 --> 06:34.984
The question now is,
do we annihilate the enemy fleet?

06:35.195 --> 06:37.857
Or do we aim to reach
the other side?

06:38.298 --> 06:39.765
It's a difficult decision.

06:40.267 --> 06:41.768
However...

06:41.768 --> 06:44.004
...I think you've already
made up your mind.

06:44.004 --> 06:46.564
We will annihilate the enemy fleet.

06:46.773 --> 06:49.833
That's what we came here for.

06:52.646 --> 06:53.513
In that case...

06:53.513 --> 06:55.749
...I suggest we switch
from Plan 1 of...

06:55.749 --> 06:58.809
...Operation Phantom Flame
to Plan 18.

07:01.188 --> 07:03.323
I believe Plan 18 is to...

07:03.323 --> 07:07.227
...make the area around the
Aptic Gate the main battlefield.

07:07.227 --> 07:08.251
That's correct.

07:08.495 --> 07:10.263
The main forces of
Operation Phantom Flame...

07:10.263 --> 07:12.754
...will be concentrated in the
Dalmav Planetary System.

07:13.233 --> 07:14.234
Given that...

07:14.234 --> 07:16.636
...I believe the
United Mankind has...

07:16.636 --> 07:18.501
...two potential routes
for an advance.

07:20.741 --> 07:23.443
From the Miofrantia Gate
to the Mystel Gate.

07:23.443 --> 07:26.412
And from the Wimpel Gate
to the Aptic Gate.

07:27.080 --> 07:29.049
At the Miofrantia and
Wimpel Gates...

07:29.049 --> 07:31.618
...we'll station some forces...

07:31.618 --> 07:34.485
...to establish defenses in the
Mystel and Aptic Systems.

07:35.422 --> 07:38.825
Whichever of those two routes
the enemy chooses to take...

07:38.825 --> 07:41.561
...we should launch an attack
using a pincer formation...

07:41.561 --> 07:44.121
...with the main forces
coming from Dalmav.

07:44.998 --> 07:49.367
That is, if our defense forces hold
out long enough for us to get there.

07:50.504 --> 07:54.031
All right.
There's nothing more to say.

07:54.875 --> 07:58.606
I want you to issue orders to
initiate Plan 18 immediately.

07:58.979 --> 08:02.779
There's one final item
that requires your decision.

08:03.450 --> 08:07.045
Who do you want to lead the
defenses at Mystel and Aptic?

08:07.888 --> 08:11.824
For the Mystel System,
Admiral Mulusufa will do the job.

08:12.859 --> 08:14.417
For the Aptic System...

08:15.362 --> 08:17.990
...we can have Admiral Bebaus
head up that fleet.

08:18.265 --> 08:20.665
I understand your choice
of Mulusufa.

08:20.967 --> 08:22.594
But Bebaus and his brother?

08:25.172 --> 08:27.402
Nereis, we've received our orders.

08:29.075 --> 08:30.440
Are they honorable?

08:30.911 --> 08:32.012
Backup Patrol Ship Sukakau
I think so.

08:32.012 --> 08:35.081
Backup Patrol Ship Sukakau
The commander-in-chief has
ordered us to defend Aptic.

08:35.081 --> 08:36.048
The commander-in-chief has
ordered us to defend Aptic.

08:37.284 --> 08:39.582
That sounds like a
pretty important job.

08:39.920 --> 08:42.556
Isn't Aptic one of the systems
they expect...

08:42.556 --> 08:44.183
...will become a major battlefield?

08:45.625 --> 08:46.592
You'll be okay.

08:47.194 --> 08:48.786
I think you can do it.

08:49.162 --> 08:51.164
If you're about to do
something stupid...

08:51.164 --> 08:53.325
...I'll put you back
on the right track.

08:54.000 --> 08:55.558
You've got it the other way around.

08:55.969 --> 08:58.605
I don't want you giving
me some dumb advice...

08:58.605 --> 09:00.573
...and embarrassing me.

09:01.441 --> 09:03.807
I suppose you think you're
the paragon of common sense.

09:04.077 --> 09:05.442
Right, Nereis?

09:05.846 --> 09:08.337
Are you saying I haven't got any,
Nefee?

09:09.182 --> 09:13.016
Your biggest problem is that
you've got little self-awareness.

09:13.820 --> 09:15.788
That would be you.

09:16.156 --> 09:18.249
You should just realize it.

09:19.826 --> 09:21.261
Anyone with common sense...

09:21.261 --> 09:23.092
...wouldn't have done
such a thing.

09:24.097 --> 09:24.722
What thing?

09:26.500 --> 09:27.801
Come on.

09:27.801 --> 09:29.936
If you can't think of an example...

09:29.936 --> 09:32.606
...maybe you shouldn't
even mention it.

09:32.606 --> 09:34.039
No...

09:34.274 --> 09:37.539
...I was trying to think
of the best example.

09:38.278 --> 09:40.109
Oh, I know which one.

09:41.648 --> 09:44.014
You don't have to try
so hard to remember.

09:44.317 --> 09:46.253
Try hard to remember?

09:46.253 --> 09:47.454
You've got that wrong.

09:47.454 --> 09:49.513
I can't forget it.

09:49.756 --> 09:51.825
Tell me, for the record.

09:51.825 --> 09:53.224
Just what did you remember?

09:53.793 --> 09:56.455
That strategy meeting we had
during our last training exercise.

09:57.531 --> 10:01.934
You gave a long speech about
the need for passion in battle.

10:02.602 --> 10:05.901
Do you remember all those
blank faces in the room?

10:06.573 --> 10:09.007
I didn't say anything wrong.

10:09.976 --> 10:13.639
I can't stand the thought that
battles are only about winning.

10:15.649 --> 10:18.752
Battles need heart.

10:18.752 --> 10:20.686
But you're not thinking rationally.

10:21.154 --> 10:22.553
Wars need to be fought.

10:22.956 --> 10:24.480
We must win on the battlefield.

10:24.791 --> 10:28.488
But one must win with style.

10:28.962 --> 10:30.361
Don't you agree?

10:33.733 --> 10:36.201
Anyway, it's time
to prepare for departure.

10:36.636 --> 10:41.164
It's a waste of time trying to talk
seriously with you about this.

10:42.175 --> 10:44.268
At last you say something sensible.

10:44.878 --> 10:47.176
Better get up to the bridge.

10:47.480 --> 10:49.950
I want to hear those orders
sending us...

10:49.950 --> 10:52.953
...to the Aptic System directly
from the commander himself.

10:52.953 --> 10:54.079
Right.

10:55.922 --> 11:00.222
It seems that my chief of staff
doesn't like those brothers.

11:01.027 --> 11:01.761
No, sir.

11:01.761 --> 11:05.128
My personal feelings about them
aren't a factor.

11:05.799 --> 11:07.460
It's a question of competency.

11:07.734 --> 11:11.571
I picked them because I believe
they have the ability.

11:11.571 --> 11:13.373
Don't worry.

11:13.373 --> 11:17.043
But if you're wrong, our entire
fleet will risk destruction.

11:17.043 --> 11:20.638
What are you so worried about?

11:21.314 --> 11:22.849
For a start, Admiral Bebaus...

11:22.849 --> 11:24.718
...doesn't have any
battle experience.

11:24.718 --> 11:29.723
He has to get his
experience sometime.

11:29.723 --> 11:31.588
This is a good opportunity.

11:32.192 --> 11:34.023
But this isn't just an exercise.

11:34.794 --> 11:40.500
We need more commanders
that have real battle experience.

11:40.500 --> 11:41.728
Besides...

11:42.869 --> 11:46.906
...I think you should trust my
judgment a little more.

11:46.906 --> 11:48.708
We, the Abriels...

11:48.708 --> 11:53.338
...have been successfully
running the Empire, after all.

11:53.513 --> 11:57.784
And I'm the one who's been
chosen for the Imperial Throne.

11:57.784 --> 12:01.743
That's right. I work so
closely with Your Highness...

12:01.955 --> 12:04.423
...that somehow I tend
to forget that.

12:04.991 --> 12:07.619
It's extremely odd.

12:08.528 --> 12:11.665
When I heard the gossip about
our new commanding officer...

12:11.665 --> 12:13.724
...I was still not aware...

12:14.134 --> 12:17.671
...that the Admiral, Prince Nereis
of Bebaus Alon Nerem...

12:17.671 --> 12:22.242
...and his Chief of Staff, Prince
Nefee of Bebaus Alon Nerem...

12:22.242 --> 12:24.711
...were from a family that
came to be known...

12:24.711 --> 12:27.339
...as the clan of
"Spectacular Insanity".

12:29.816 --> 12:32.652
Of all the admirals they
could've chosen...

12:32.652 --> 12:34.950
...we had to get this one.

12:35.155 --> 12:37.157
Be that as it may...

12:37.157 --> 12:39.192
...whoever the commander is...

12:39.192 --> 12:42.457
...it doesn't make any difference
to the crew on an assault ship.

12:44.597 --> 12:47.031
Brave of you to see it that way.

12:47.333 --> 12:51.064
I'm sure all the other pilots
are shaking in their boots.

12:52.639 --> 12:54.334
What's that supposed to mean?

12:55.375 --> 12:58.778
I'm afraid your time for
requisitioning spare parts...

12:58.778 --> 12:59.904
...has just expired.

13:00.113 --> 13:01.948
But wait a minute!

13:01.948 --> 13:04.644
You're closing the books on me
because of a little gossip?

13:06.453 --> 13:07.920
This is terrible.

13:08.188 --> 13:11.357
In the end, I wasn't able to get
the replacement parts...

13:11.357 --> 13:13.518
...for the laser cannon.

13:14.461 --> 13:17.731
If we're called into battle
before our next supply...

13:17.731 --> 13:20.325
...how are we going to manage
at half capacity?

13:20.600 --> 13:21.259
Hey!

13:23.603 --> 13:24.938
Samson!

13:24.938 --> 13:27.236
Are you two heading out
on a date?

13:28.041 --> 13:28.837
"You two"?

13:30.777 --> 13:33.613
Let's have a toast to our
bright futures!

13:33.613 --> 13:35.682
And to the Spectacular Insanity!

13:35.682 --> 13:37.650
A toast with a Surugu?

13:37.650 --> 13:39.811
Doesn't matter if it's
from the heart!

13:40.253 --> 13:41.020
I was wondering...

13:41.020 --> 13:44.649
...what is this
"Spectacular Insanity" anyway?

13:45.158 --> 13:47.592
Didn't you learn
about it in school?

13:49.028 --> 13:52.365
I did learn that
the Bebaus family...

13:52.365 --> 13:54.560
...is one of the twenty-nine
root families.

13:54.901 --> 13:56.202
One ancestor...

13:56.202 --> 13:59.973
...was instrumental in developing
Plane Space technology...

13:59.973 --> 14:03.431
...and the family has produced
lots of great scientists.

14:05.011 --> 14:07.377
That's only one side of the story.

14:08.681 --> 14:10.383
You see...

14:10.383 --> 14:13.019
...any family that has a lot of
geniuses in its ranks...

14:13.019 --> 14:16.580
...is also likely to have some
who are on the crazy side.

14:17.190 --> 14:21.684
But didn't Admiral Bebaus come from
a good branch of the family tree?

14:23.263 --> 14:25.128
You don't understand.

14:25.331 --> 14:28.034
Not even his branch of
the family has escaped...

14:28.034 --> 14:30.603
...this colorful part of their history.

14:30.603 --> 14:34.140
So the nickname people give
to this colorful history is...

14:34.140 --> 14:36.509
..."Spectacular Insanity."

14:36.509 --> 14:37.944
But still...

14:37.944 --> 14:41.548
...it shouldn't matter if the admiral
is a bit on the crazy side.

14:41.548 --> 14:44.278
Not if he's surrounded
with intelligent staff.

14:44.484 --> 14:45.746
You see...

14:46.052 --> 14:49.122
I've heard people say his
chief of staff is also a Bebaus.

14:49.122 --> 14:50.350
So there.

14:53.893 --> 14:55.417
Aviator Samson!

14:57.197 --> 14:59.666
What's the matter, Petty Officer?

14:59.666 --> 15:01.793
What do you mean?

15:02.001 --> 15:05.835
I bet you forgot to turn
on your Clyuno again.

15:06.139 --> 15:09.700
I had no idea where you were,
so I've been looking for you!

15:11.411 --> 15:13.845
Well, it's not like I forgot.

15:14.280 --> 15:18.351
Sometimes it's important for
a crewmember to search for...

15:18.351 --> 15:20.553
You've used that excuse
three times!

15:20.553 --> 15:22.953
You'd better come up
with something new.

15:23.389 --> 15:27.553
Well, guess that means this is
the end of my little break.

15:28.061 --> 15:30.430
Stay a while longer
and enjoy yourselves.

15:30.430 --> 15:30.725
What?

15:35.034 --> 15:35.898
See ya!

15:38.338 --> 15:40.203
What did he mean by "you two"?

15:41.674 --> 15:42.163
Hey...

15:43.643 --> 15:44.871
What is it?

15:45.812 --> 15:48.848
Why didn't you bring your cat
this time?

15:48.848 --> 15:50.042
Oh, uh...

15:50.884 --> 15:54.120
I thought it would be better if he
stayed onboard the Basroil.

15:54.120 --> 15:57.419
His duty is to catch mice up there.

15:59.626 --> 16:01.427
In any case...

16:01.427 --> 16:03.796
...you really seem to like cats.

16:03.796 --> 16:05.698
You're always fussing over mine.

16:05.698 --> 16:06.790
I hate cats.

16:07.867 --> 16:08.492
What? Why?

16:09.102 --> 16:11.604
We always had lots of cats
back at home.

16:11.604 --> 16:14.007
There were always lots of
kittens around.

16:14.007 --> 16:17.499
But they bullied me because
I was the only human.

16:17.977 --> 16:19.740
They bullied you?

16:19.946 --> 16:21.038
The cats?!

16:21.247 --> 16:23.272
What else do you think
I'm talking about?

16:23.516 --> 16:27.350
Then why do you fuss over
my cat so much?

16:27.553 --> 16:28.918
Because he's your cat.

16:29.455 --> 16:30.183
Huh?

16:31.724 --> 16:34.022
So, does that make you happy?

16:36.629 --> 16:38.062
I suppose...

16:39.198 --> 16:40.893
Our break's over.

16:41.701 --> 16:42.963
I'm going back to the ship.

16:43.403 --> 16:45.571
It's already that time?

16:45.571 --> 16:48.563
I guess I'd better go and
see the captain...

16:51.444 --> 16:52.312
What's wrong?

16:52.312 --> 16:54.180
Uh, I'm sorry. It's just that...

16:54.180 --> 16:56.842
...if anyone saw us here like this...

16:58.785 --> 17:00.013
Lafiel?!

17:00.553 --> 17:02.418
It seems I came at the right time.

17:03.189 --> 17:05.792
The repairs to the Basroil
are complete.

17:05.792 --> 17:08.094
The flying section is ready
to go back on duty.

17:08.094 --> 17:10.596
Second Aviator,
resume your position.

17:10.596 --> 17:11.824
Yes, Captain.

17:12.932 --> 17:16.026
I need to go to operational
headquarters now.

17:17.103 --> 17:19.196
W-Wait a minute. Lafiel...

17:20.139 --> 17:21.441
Tenth time...

17:21.441 --> 17:22.373
Lafiel!

17:24.310 --> 17:27.347
I thought you were off-duty now.

17:27.347 --> 17:29.349
There's no need to tag along.

17:29.349 --> 17:31.551
I know. It's just I...

17:31.551 --> 17:33.586
...I just wanted to talk to you.

17:33.586 --> 17:34.487
Very well.

17:34.487 --> 17:35.977
Come with me, then.

17:36.622 --> 17:37.890
Darn.

17:37.890 --> 17:39.687
She must have seen it.

17:41.527 --> 17:45.331
Hey, do you know anything
about Admiral Bebaus?

17:45.331 --> 17:47.567
He's in charge of defending
the whole Aptic System!

17:47.567 --> 17:49.068
Of course I do...

17:49.068 --> 17:52.970
Don't forget, the Abriels are one
of the twenty-nine root families.

17:53.406 --> 17:56.898
I know both Admiral Nereis and
his chief of staff Nefee very well.

17:57.910 --> 17:59.445
Are they from the same family?

17:59.445 --> 18:01.538
Apparently they are identical twins.

18:01.814 --> 18:03.975
Identical twins?

18:04.550 --> 18:07.420
Didn't the Abh have control
over their children's births?

18:07.420 --> 18:10.223
Their parents must've
chosen to have twins.

18:10.223 --> 18:14.394
Parents normally think raising
children with the exact same...

18:14.394 --> 18:16.794
...genetic structure is not
a good idea.

18:17.530 --> 18:19.395
But they are the Bebaus family,
after all.

18:19.599 --> 18:23.102
They probably did it just because
it was unique.

18:23.102 --> 18:24.771
Right.

18:24.771 --> 18:28.104
But, even though they're twins,
they have different ranks.

18:29.442 --> 18:33.037
Why am I going on like this?

18:34.414 --> 18:36.315
A person with many loves
will not be promoted.

18:36.315 --> 18:36.940
What?

18:37.950 --> 18:39.685
Apparently Admiral Nereis...

18:39.685 --> 18:42.916
...says that to his chief of staff
Nefee all the time.

18:44.624 --> 18:45.147
Oh, right.

18:45.358 --> 18:46.726
Of course...

18:46.726 --> 18:51.697
...according to Nefee,
Admiral Nereis is merely...

18:51.697 --> 18:53.824
...letting his relationship
continue under its own inertia.

18:55.368 --> 18:55.993
Jinto!

18:56.202 --> 18:56.998
What?

18:57.470 --> 19:00.803
You express your thoughts
too clearly on your face.

19:01.274 --> 19:02.002
Huh?

19:02.308 --> 19:05.835
You weren't hoping that I'd think
it was a misunderstanding?

19:07.680 --> 19:08.544
All right.

19:08.981 --> 19:10.817
I surrender, Lafiel!

19:10.817 --> 19:13.152
With the tactics you
just used on me...

19:13.152 --> 19:15.855
...I'm sure you'll become
an admiral one day.

19:15.855 --> 19:19.058
Well, your prediction
will be accurate.

19:19.058 --> 19:19.956
Now, then...

19:20.526 --> 19:22.228
...after I'm done at headquarters...

19:22.228 --> 19:23.896
...I'll be taking my break.

19:23.896 --> 19:27.024
If you're interested,
you may accompany me.

19:29.235 --> 19:31.226
Sure. I'd love to...

19:32.472 --> 19:34.770
...Admiral Abriel.

19:39.312 --> 19:42.715
Our short break helped us forget
for a while...

19:42.715 --> 19:46.116
...the difficulties that lay ahead
in the upcoming battle.

19:48.154 --> 19:49.222
However...

19:49.222 --> 19:51.557
...once I was back on the Basroil...

19:51.557 --> 19:54.527
...something major
happened so quickly...

19:54.527 --> 19:55.824
...that it brought us
back to reality.

20:00.600 --> 20:02.435
Supply Officer Lin?

20:02.435 --> 20:03.060
What is it?

20:03.769 --> 20:04.701
Is your cat okay?

20:05.138 --> 20:08.335
Yeah, I think he's doing fine.

20:08.975 --> 20:10.643
You called just for that?

20:10.643 --> 20:11.439
No.

20:11.744 --> 20:13.678
There's an outside transmission
for you.

20:13.946 --> 20:15.880
Well, that's unusual.

20:16.149 --> 20:16.911
Who's it from?

20:17.150 --> 20:18.048
Headquarters.

20:18.251 --> 20:18.683
What?

20:18.851 --> 20:20.011
I'll put you through.

20:21.420 --> 20:23.089
From Commander Atosuryua?!

20:23.089 --> 20:23.987
Wait a minute!

20:25.892 --> 20:28.861
Good morning,
Supply Officer Lin.

20:28.861 --> 20:31.125
Good morning to you too,
Commander!

20:31.497 --> 20:34.300
I'd like to see you when
I'm talking to you.

20:34.300 --> 20:35.699
Uh, right away.

20:38.938 --> 20:41.741
No need for you to be so formal.

20:41.741 --> 20:44.544
I'm calling you on a
purely personal matter.

20:44.544 --> 20:45.811
Really?

20:45.811 --> 20:48.447
So, how can I help you?

20:48.447 --> 20:51.918
I wanted to invite you and
Captain Abriel for dinner.

20:51.918 --> 20:54.754
I've made reservations at a
restaurant called Mitsugoiwa.

20:54.754 --> 20:57.957
It's probably not the most
appropriate place in which to...

20:57.957 --> 21:00.793
...entertain a princess and a count.

21:00.793 --> 21:03.729
Nevertheless, it is by far the
best place to eat in Dakul...

21:03.729 --> 21:05.331
...and we are in a war zone.

21:05.331 --> 21:07.266
I hope you don't mind.

21:07.266 --> 21:08.935
A dinner invitation?

21:08.935 --> 21:09.867
But why?

21:10.703 --> 21:14.373
I'm inviting you and
Captain Abriel.

21:14.373 --> 21:15.635
Don't you get it?

21:16.242 --> 21:19.973
Does this have anything to do
with the death of your brother?

21:20.346 --> 21:21.480
Yes.

21:21.480 --> 21:25.746
Tomorrow would have been my
brother's birthday if he were alive.

21:25.918 --> 21:28.554
Obviously he can't be here
to celebrate, so...

21:28.554 --> 21:32.091
...I want to have a party with people
who had a connection with him.

21:32.091 --> 21:33.359
But...

21:33.359 --> 21:36.996
...while there might be a connection,
it isn't the right kind.

21:36.996 --> 21:38.164
I mean...

21:38.164 --> 21:40.967
I understand your concerns...

21:40.967 --> 21:42.434
...but the past is the past.

21:42.702 --> 21:45.104
The only people who knew
my brother in this star system...

21:45.104 --> 21:47.004
...are you two and me.

21:47.406 --> 21:50.276
You're not suggesting I celebrate
his birthday all by myself?

21:50.276 --> 21:52.211
I wasn't saying that, but...

21:52.211 --> 21:53.179
All right.

21:53.179 --> 21:55.647
Now, I've got a favor to ask you.

21:57.016 --> 21:59.118
I want you to extend
this invitation...

21:59.118 --> 22:01.520
...to Captain Abriel...

22:01.520 --> 22:04.957
...or rather, to Viscountess Paryunu,
on my behalf.

22:04.957 --> 22:10.263
I realize that it's my duty
to personally invite her...

22:10.263 --> 22:11.864
...but you know...

22:11.864 --> 22:13.599
...this is a rather personal issue...
- Which means that...

22:13.599 --> 22:15.794
...if Lafiel refuses this invitation...

22:16.435 --> 22:18.537
...I can avoid going as well.

22:18.537 --> 22:19.538
I'm sure you can...

22:19.538 --> 22:21.641
I understand. I will go and...

22:21.641 --> 22:26.445
Of course, even if the Princess
refuses, you'll still come, right?

22:26.445 --> 22:26.968
What?!

22:27.613 --> 22:30.182
I'd hate to have to
cancel my reservation.

22:30.182 --> 22:31.581
That would be embarrassing.

22:32.752 --> 22:34.583
Of course!

22:35.421 --> 22:39.759
Make sure you tell her that
this is a personal invitation.

22:39.759 --> 22:41.693
Okay! I'll be counting on you!

22:44.764 --> 22:49.335
This time, I couldn't help...

22:49.335 --> 22:51.599
...cursing myself for my
own sheepishness.

22:54.240 --> 22:58.540
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.178 --> 23:03.342
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.684 --> 23:08.279
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.488 --> 23:13.322
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.526 --> 23:15.795
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.795 --> 23:19.561
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.966 --> 23:26.105
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:26.105 --> 23:29.666
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.076 --> 23:34.069
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.613 --> 23:39.251
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.251 --> 23:46.325
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.325 --> 23:51.497
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.497 --> 24:00.030
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.007 --> 24:07.146
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.146 --> 24:12.418
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.418 --> 24:20.917
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.360 --> 24:25.626
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.103 --> 24:34.197
I understand your concerns...

24:34.874 --> 24:36.475
...but what's past is past.

24:36.475 --> 24:39.445
Who knows?
Maybe it was a lover of his...

24:39.445 --> 24:44.007
I had to leave your brother's
dinner party in the middle of it.

24:44.817 --> 24:46.919
So, a battle in normal space...

24:46.919 --> 24:48.854
It's not very edifying...

24:48.854 --> 24:52.984
...considering we have the power
to roam around in Plane Space.

24:53.325 --> 24:55.961
As long as the result is dramatic,
it'll be fine.

24:55.961 --> 24:57.863
But that's not our sole objective...

24:57.863 --> 24:58.564
Next Episode...
Remembrance Dinner
But that's not our sole objective...

24:58.564 --> 25:00.599
Next Episode...
Remembrance Dinner
...my dear brother.

25:00.599 --> 25:00.997
Next Episode...
Remembrance Dinner
